### YCR API — every endpoint in F-001.
###
### READ THIS FIRST — why most of these return 401.
###
### ADR-0020 ships the authorization pipeline in F-001 but **no authentication handler**. The
### only handler in the repository lives in tests/YCR.Api.Tests and is registered exclusively
### through WebApplicationFactory.ConfigureTestServices; spec S21a asserts no
### AuthenticationHandler<> subtype exists anywhere in src/, and S21b has startup refuse an
### unexpected scheme outside the Testing environment.
###
### So, against a locally running API:
###   - /health/live and /health/ready answer 200. They are the only anonymous endpoints
###     (docs/20 §4 requires an explicit .AllowAnonymous() with a reason).
###   - every /api/v1/stations request answers **401**. There is no credential to send and
###     **no dev-auth mechanism is provided**, deliberately: a "just for local development"
###     bypass is exactly the kind of thing that survives into a deployment.
###
### The 2xx/4xx behaviours below are proven by tests/YCR.Api.Tests, which host the same
### Program with the test handler attached. This file documents the surface and lets you
### confirm the 401s are real; it is not a way to work around them. Real credentials arrive
### with the ADR-0016 token feature that ADR-0020 defers.
###
### OpenAPI document (Development environment only): {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

@host = http://localhost:5080
@stationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Liveness probe — expect 200. Anonymous.
GET {{host}}/health/live

### Readiness probe — expect 200, or 503 when the database is unreachable. Anonymous.
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### OpenAPI document — expect 200 in Development, 404 otherwise.
### Not served outside Development: the document maps every route and the permission each one
### requires, which a deployed instance has no reason to hand out.
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

### Create a station — expect 401 (no authentication handler; requires stations.manage).
### With a credential: 201 + Location, or 400 / 409 Network.StationCodeAlreadyExists.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "INS",
  "nameEn": "Insein",
  "nameMy": "အင်းစိန်"
}

### Create a station with an invalid code — expect 401 here; 400 Network.InvalidStationCode
### with a credential. The code rule (R3) lives only in StationCode and is provisional until
### OQ26 is answered.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "in-s",
  "nameEn": "Insein",
  "nameMy": "အင်းစိန်"
}

### Create a station with a missing field — expect 401 here; 400 Common.ValidationFailed with
### a credential. Rejected by the endpoint filter before the handler runs.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "INS",
  "nameEn": "Insein"
}

### List stations — expect 401 (requires stations.read). With a credential: 200 with
### { items, page, pageSize, totalCount }, ordered by code.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stations?page=1&pageSize=50

### List stations above the page-size cap — expect 401 here; 400 Network.InvalidPageRequest
### with a credential. docs/20 §4 caps pageSize at 200.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stations?page=1&pageSize=201

### Read one station — expect 401 (requires stations.read). With a credential: 200, or
### 404 Network.StationNotFound.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/stations/{{stationId}}

### Deactivate a station — expect 401 (requires stations.manage). With a credential: 204,
### 404 Network.StationNotFound, or 422 Network.StationAlreadyInactive.
### The row is retained, so the code is never reused (R3).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/stations/{{stationId}}/deactivate
